.TH XTED 1 "November 2026" "xted" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xted, xt \- terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xted
.RI [ file [: line [: column ]]]\ ...
.br
.B xted
.B \-
.br
.B xted
.I directory
.br
.B xted
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xted
is a text editor for the terminal, written in C99 with nothing but the POSIX C library: no
ncurses, no terminfo, no other library.
It is a single binary that starts in under 50 ms.
.B xt
is a short name for the same program (a link made by
.BR "make install" ).
.PP
The editor is not modal and uses familiar shortcuts (Ctrl+S, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+Z).
For programming it has syntax highlighting, automatic indentation, suggestions of the symbols of
the file, of the files it includes and of the standard library (PHP, C, C++, Python,
JavaScript and TypeScript), snippets, multiple cursors, folding and jumps to definitions.
It needs no language server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.IR file [: line [: column ]]
Open the file, and move the cursor to the line (and column) given.
Several files are opened as several buffers, shown as tabs.
The suffix is read as a position only when no file with that exact name exists.
.TP
.B \-
Read the text from standard input (only once).
.TP
.I directory
Open the file browser on that directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\^\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.PP
Without arguments, the files that were open and the cursor positions of the last session in the
current folder are restored.
.SH KEYS
All shortcuts can be changed (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
They are listed next to each command in the command palette.
.SS Files and buffers
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save.
.B Alt+S
saves as,
.B Alt+A
saves all.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Quick open: fuzzy search of the files of the project.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
List of the buffers.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the buffer.
.B Alt+.\&
and
.B Alt+,
(or
.B Ctrl+PgDn
and
.BR Ctrl+PgUp )
go to the next and the previous buffer.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Show or hide the file browser.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SS Panes
.TP
.B Alt+\e
Split vertically.
.B Alt+\-
splits horizontally.
.TP
.B Alt+E
Resize mode (arrow keys move the border).
.TP
.B Alt+Q
Close the pane.
.TP
.BR Alt+O ", " Alt+Right ", " Ctrl+Tab
Next pane.
.BR Alt+Left " and " Ctrl+Shift+Tab
go to the previous one.
.SS Search and navigation
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Find, incrementally.
.B Ctrl+R
replaces,
.B Alt+F
searches in the files of the project.
.TP
.BR F3 ", " Alt+N
Next match.
.BR Shift+F3 " and " Alt+P
go to the previous one.
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
Go to a line (and column).
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Go to a symbol: classes, functions, methods, properties and constants of the file.
.TP
.B F12
Go to the definition, with a
.B tags
file made by ctags.
.TP
.B Alt+M
Matching bracket.
.SS Editing
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Z ", " Ctrl+Y
Undo, redo.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+A ", " Alt+L ", " Alt+W
Select all, the line, the word.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+C ", " Ctrl+X ", " Ctrl+V
Copy, cut, paste.
.B Alt+V
pastes the previous entry of the history.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+K ", " Ctrl+J
Delete lines, join lines.
.TP
.BR Alt+Up ", " Alt+Down
Move the line up or down.
.B Alt+Y
duplicates it.
.TP
.B Alt+/
Comment or uncomment.
.TP
.B Alt+K
Filter the selection through a shell command.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Indent or unindent.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+D ", " Alt+D
Add a cursor at the next occurrence of the word, or at all of them.
.B Alt+Shift+Up
and
.B Alt+Shift+Down
add a cursor above or below.
.TP
.B Alt+Z
Fold or unfold the block.
.SS Running commands
.TP
.B Alt+R
Run a shell command; the output appears in an
.B [Output]
pane.
.B F5
repeats it,
.B Shift+F5
stops it.
.TP
.BR F8 ", " Shift+F8
Next and previous error (the
.I file:line:column
format of gcc, tsc, Python).
.SS Other
.TP
.B F1
Help: every command with its keys (the ones in use, also those changed in the configuration),
the keys of the lists, of the search bar and of the suggestions, and the files the editor uses.
.TP
.B Alt+X
Command palette.
.TP
.B Alt+T
Change the theme.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Redraw the screen.
.SH SEARCH BAR
While the search bar is open:
.B Alt+C
switches case sensitivity,
.B Alt+W
whole words and
.B Alt+R
regular expressions (POSIX extended).
.B Enter
accepts,
.B Esc
cancels.
The keys that can be used are shown at the right of the bar.
When replacing, each match asks
.RB \(lq "Replace? (y = yes, n = no, a = all, Esc = done)" \(rq.
.SH COMMAND PALETTE
.B Alt+X
lists all the commands, narrowed down while a part of the name is typed.
With an empty search the commands are in sections: first the actions, then the settings that
change the behavior of the editor.
Each row shows the name, the present value of a setting (a filled circle when it is on) and
all the shortcuts of the command.
.B Enter
on an action runs it and closes the palette; on a setting it changes it and leaves the palette
open.
.PP
The settings are: mouse, autosuggest, automatic pairs of brackets and quotes, Git markers,
system clipboard, indentation (tab, 2, 4 or 8 spaces), theme and language (with the catalog file
in use).
.B Save settings...\&
writes the choices into a configuration file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Everything has a default: the editor works with no configuration.
The folder is
.IB $XDG_CONFIG_HOME /xted
or
.BR ~/.config/xted :
.TP
.B config
Settings and shortcuts.
.TP
.B syntax/
More languages, one file each, in the format described at the top of
.BR src/langs.c .
.TP
.B themes/
More color themes, one file each.
.TP
.B lang/
Translation catalogs, one file per language.
.SS The config file
Lines of
.IR key " = " value ,
comments with
.BR # .
Keys before the first section apply to all languages; a section
.RI [ Language ]
changes them for that language;
.B [keys]
holds the shortcuts.
.TP
.B theme
.B dark
(default),
.B light
or a theme of your own.
.TP
.BR mouse ", " git ", " clipboard
.BR on " or " off .
The clipboard setting also sends the copies to the system clipboard (OSC 52).
.TP
.B language
.BR auto " (from the environment), " en ", " it
or the code of any catalog found.
.TP
.BR tab_width ", " indent_width
Width of a tab, and spaces of one indentation level (1 to 16).
.TP
.B expand_tab
Tab inserts spaces.
.TP
.B trim_trailing_space
Remove the trailing spaces when saving.
.TP
.B final_newline
.BR keep " or " always .
.TP
.BR autosuggest ", " autopair
Suggestions while typing, and automatic closing brackets and quotes.
.TP
.B suggest_min
Letters typed before the suggestions appear (1 to 10).
.PP
In the
.B [keys]
section a line such as
.B ctrl+shift+d = duplicate_down
binds a key to a command; the value
.B none
removes a shortcut.
.SS The project file
A file called
.B .xted
in the folder of the project (or above the files) has the same format.
Its language keys win over the user's file for the documents of the project; its global keys
(theme, mouse, git, clipboard, language) are read at start from the one nearest to the first file.
.SS Order of precedence
For the settings of a document: a command given in the session, the project's
.BR .xted ,
the user's file,
.BR .editorconfig ,
the style found in the text (tabs or spaces), the defaults.
.PP
.B .editorconfig
is read from the folder of the file upwards:
.BR indent_style ,
.BR indent_size ,
.BR tab_width ,
.B trim_trailing_whitespace
and
.BR insert_final_newline .
.SS Saving the settings
.B Save settings...\&
in the palette asks where to write what was changed with commands: the user's file, the
project's
.BR .xted ,
or
.B .editorconfig
(indentation only).
Files are changed line by line and written atomically, so comments and order are kept.
.SH LANGUAGE
The texts of the editor are English in the code and are translated from catalogs, which are text
files and not part of the binary.
A catalog is named after the language (\c
.BR it ).
It has a line per text: the English text, a tab, the translation;
.B #
starts a comment,
.B @name
gives the name of the language, and
.BR \e\^n ,
.B \et
and
.B \e\e
are escapes.
A translation whose
.BR printf (3)
conversions differ from the original is ignored.
.PP
Catalogs are searched in
.BR ~/.config/xted/lang/ ,
in
.B lang/
and
.B ../share/xted/lang/
next to the executable, and in
.BR $PREFIX/share/xted/lang/ .
If the language or its file is missing, English is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/xted/config
User configuration.
.TP
.B .xted
Configuration of a project.
.TP
.B .editorconfig
Read for indentation, trailing spaces and final newline.
.TP
.B tags
A ctags file, used by the jump to the definition.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/xted/sessions/
One file per folder from which the editor was started, with the open files and the cursors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base folder of the configuration (default
.BR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base folder of the sessions (default
.BR ~/.local/state ).
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Choose the language when
.B language = auto
(for example
.B it_IT.UTF-8
is Italian).
.TP
.BR COLORTERM ", " TERM
Decide whether colors are truecolor, 256 or 16.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns the colors off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be opened, or there is no interactive terminal.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong option or use.
.SH NOTES
.B xted
always puts the terminal back as it was, also on
.BR SIGTERM ,
.B SIGHUP
or a crash.
Ctrl+C is the copy shortcut and does not interrupt the program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctags (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR vi (1),
.BR nano (1)
.PP
The full documentation is in the files
.B README.md
and
.B SPEC.md
of the source tree.
